  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1100 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nWednesday through Saturday:\n\nLate Wednesday into Thanksgiving uncertainty really increases \nas the high pressure nudges and a new system develops and nudges\nin. The uncertainty with this next potential event on \nThanksgiving appears to be primarily driven by the development \nand track of the upper level trough/closed low in addition to \nits interaction with a developing nor'easter system in the gulf \nthat will swing up the eastern seaboard. This is apparent when \nlooking at the cluster analysis in addition to individual \nmodels. Ultimately the upper levels will be the critical aspect \nwhen it comes to how Thanksgiving plays out. However, there will\nbe precip chances with this, perhaps even some light \naccumulating snow. The best chances appear to be closer to the \nlake as of right now with potential for some lake enhancement. \nThis will be the situation to monitor over the next few days as \nmodels dial in on how the upper levels may play out. \n\nOtherwise a brief late week system Friday/Saturday looks \npossible as well but this looks to be a weak, fast moving \nclipper with limited moisture, but could bring some rain/snow \nmix if things come together in the moisture field a bit better. \nThe way things have trended is wetter overall for this late week\nperiod with little to no break between Thanksgiving and \nFriday/Saturday clipper but much of this relies upon a very \nuncertain Thanksgiving storm situation. \n\nKuroski",
